        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac35P(B)=\\dfrac3{10}P(A)$, so $P(A)=2P(B)$.\n\nExpress $P(A\\cap B)$ using each conditional probability and equate the expressions.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(A\\cap B)&=\\frac35P(B)\\\\P(A\\cap B)&=\\frac3{10}P(A)\\end{align*}$$\nEquating these expressions gives\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac3{10}P(A)&=\\frac35P(B)\\\\P(A)&=2P(B)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p34-q24b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p34-q24b-prompt",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
