              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Find the value of ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "P(A)",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ".",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$P(A)=\\dfrac14$.\n\nUse $P(A\\cup B)=1-\\dfrac7{10}$, with $P(B)=\\dfrac12P(A)$ and $P(A\\cap B)=\\dfrac3{10}P(A)$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(A\\cup B)&=1-P(\\overline{A}\\cap\\overline{B})\\\\P(A\\cup B)&=1-\\frac7{10}\\\\P(A\\cup B)&=\\frac3{10}\\end{align*}$$\nFrom part (a), $P(B)=\\frac12P(A)$, and $P(A\\cap B)=\\frac3{10}P(A)$. The addition rule gives\n$$\\begin{align*}P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B)&=\\frac3{10}\\\\P(A)+\\frac12P(A)-\\frac3{10}P(A)&=\\frac3{10}\\\\\\frac65P(A)&=\\frac3{10}\\\\P(A)&=\\frac14\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 74
      },
      {
        "id": "p34-q24c",
